<h1 class="article-title">Liepāja SEZ Authority’s 2026 Budget Focuses on Development</h1>
<div class="block_text mt-5 mb-4">
<div class="row">
<div class="col"><div class="col-12 output"><p>The Liepāja SEZ Authority’s 2026 budget has been prepared conservatively and in a balanced manner, ensuring the performance of its core functions while continuing development-oriented investment projects in the port and industrial areas. The strategic priorities for 2026 are greater operational efficiency, infrastructure construction, digital port management and stronger cybersecurity. The Liepāja SEZ Board has approved a 2026 budget with planned turnover of EUR 17.9 million.</p><p>Liepāja SEZ CEO Uldis Hmieļevskis stresses that the priority this year is to maintain stable operations in uncertain conditions. “This year we will continue work on reconstructing Berth No. 46, significantly increasing the port’s long-term competitiveness. We will continue developing infrastructure required by fishermen, constructing an access road to Berth No. 92 under a Rural Support Service project and reconstructing the berth itself. In 2026 we will continue supporting the growth and expansion of existing businesses, constructing streets and utility networks in the Liepāja Industrial Park and improving existing infrastructure. We will also continue environmentally sustainable investments, including remediation of contaminated areas at the former Liepājas metalurgs factory.” In 2026 the Authority will continue working with developers on sustainable industrial projects aimed at climate neutrality, reducing CO2 emissions and producing and using renewable energy.</p><p>The Authority’s budget revenue comes from port activities and property lease payments, as well as investment and financial activities and international projects. Expenditure covers core activities intended to boost economic activity, attract investment and maintain and construct infrastructure, creating a high-quality business environment. Finance Director Ilze Rendniece notes the importance of a balanced budget with prudent revenue and expenditure forecasts, ensuring core operating costs and the fulfilment of financial and EU project commitments.</p><p>The budget is based on a projected cargo turnover of 6.9 million tonnes in 2026 and existing property lease agreements.</p><p> </p><p>The Liepāja SEZ Authority’s 2026 budget is a financial plan for implementing its development priorities and securing the long-term competitiveness of the Liepāja Special Economic Zone as a unified economic ecosystem:</p><p>1. Maintenance and development of port infrastructure.</p><ul><li>Reconstruction of Berths No. 46, 92 and 82 at the Port of Liepāja.</li><li>Development of infrastructure for the safe mooring of RO-RO ferries.</li><li>Maintaining sufficient water depths in the port basin.</li><li>Construction of an access road for fishermen.</li><li>Maintenance of railway infrastructure, buildings and watercraft.</li></ul><p>Objective: ensure stable port operations with annual cargo turnover of 6.9 million tonnes, increase capacity and competitiveness, and attract new cargo.</p><p>2. Development of industrial areas.</p><ul><li>Construction of streets and utilities in the Liepāja Industrial Park.</li><li>Construction of sections of Martena Street and Eksporta Street.</li><li>Cleaning up and remediating industrial areas, including demolition of derelict structures.</li></ul><p>Objective: attract new investors and increase economic activity.</p><p>3. Digital transformation and cybersecurity.</p><ul><li>Creation of a digital port management system.</li><li>Digitalisation of security systems.</li><li>Measures to meet cybersecurity requirements.</li></ul><p>Objective: improve operational efficiency and reduce security risks.</p><p>4. Environmental safety and sustainability.</p><ul><li>Compliance with environmental and safety requirements.</li><li>Environmental quality monitoring in the port area.</li><li>Dismantling the fuel-oil storage facility and remediating contaminated soil at the former Liepājas metalurgs plant.</li></ul><p>Objective: ensure environmental sustainability and reduce ecological risks.</p><p>5. Financial stability and sustainability.</p><ul><li>Fulfilling existing commitments and investment projects.</li></ul><p>6. Strengthening staff qualifications and capacity.</p><ul><li>Ensuring continuity of expertise and conducting necessary certification and training.</li></ul></div>
